[TITLE]
AquaOptima dPHM-PINN Sprint 18 — small reference EPANET .inp fixture
in US-customary units WITH a [OPTIONS] Demand Multiplier directive.
Five-node looped distribution sample: one reservoir + four junctions,
five pipes. GPM flow units, Hazen-Williams head loss, Demand
Multiplier 2.0.

Mirrors epanet_reference_loop_gpm.inp exactly, except for the added
``Demand Multiplier 2.0`` row. The fallback parser must scale every
junction demand by 2.0 after the GPM -> m^3/s conversion, so the
loaded Network's positive demand sum is exactly twice that of
epanet_reference_loop_gpm.inp. Reservoir head, pipe length / diameter
/ roughness are NOT affected.

US-customary EPANET convention (per the EPANET 2.2 user manual):
  - length in feet
  - diameter in inches
  - head/elevation in feet
  - demand/flow in the [OPTIONS] Units value (here GPM)
  - Demand Multiplier scales all junction demands at load time

[JUNCTIONS]
;ID   Elev   Demand   Pattern
 J1   0.0    100.0    ;     ; 100 GPM consumer (scaled to 200 GPM)
 J2   0.0    150.0    ;     ; 150 GPM consumer (scaled to 300 GPM)
 J3   0.0    120.0    ;     ; 120 GPM consumer (scaled to 240 GPM)
 J4   0.0     80.0    ;     ;  80 GPM consumer (scaled to 160 GPM)

[RESERVOIRS]
;ID   Head   Pattern
 R1   300.0  ;          ; 300 ft fixed-head reservoir

[PIPES]
;ID   Node1   Node2   Length   Diameter   Roughness   MinorLoss   Status
 P1   R1      J1      1000.0   10.0       130.0       0.0         OPEN
 P2   J1      J2       800.0    8.0       130.0       0.0         OPEN
 P3   J2      J3       700.0    6.0       130.0       0.0         OPEN
 P4   J3      J4       650.0    6.0       130.0       0.0         OPEN
 P5   J1      J4       900.0    6.0       130.0       0.0         OPEN

[OPTIONS]
 Units                GPM
 Headloss             H-W
 Demand Multiplier    2.0

[END]
